IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc9-sch7-p2`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- SCHEDULE 6: assessment of extent of disablement (and the blank Schedule 8, "Industrial injuries and diseases (Old Cases)", which has
-- no encodable text: NOTES.md). The converter dropped the paragraph numbers. Paragraphs 1 to 3 follow the order of the text and the
-- citations "paragraph 1(c)", "paragraph 1(d) or 2"; paragraphs 4 and 5 are the two blank lines under "Severe disablement allowance";
-- 6 is "Disablement benefit" (cited as "paragraph 4 or 6 of Schedule 6" at src:5502, where 4 is the blank severe disablement allowance
-- paragraph and 6 is this one); 7 and 8 follow. The paragraph that Schedule 7 Part II calls "9(3)" is imported from ssc9-sch7-p2.

§ `Schedule 6 -- assessment of extent of disablement`

§§ `Paragraph 1 -- general provisions as to method of assessment`

-- 1(a): the disabilities to be taken into account are all disabilities incurred as a result of the relevant loss of faculty (whether or
-- not involving loss of earning power or additional expense) to which the claimant may be expected to be subject during the period taken
-- into account, compared with a person of the same age and sex whose physical and mental condition is normal. 1(b) takes out the
-- disabilities that also result from another cause, as regulations provide. "shall be" fixes the set, so a disability outside it is out.
-- src:5341 | For the purposes of section ...103 above and Part II of Schedule 7 to this Act, the extent of disablement shall be assessed, by reference to the disabilities incurred by the claimant as a result of the relevant loss of faculty, in accordance with the following general principles—
-- src:5342 | (a) except as provided in paragraphs (b) to (d) below, the disabilities to be taken into account shall be all disabilities so incurred (whether or not involving loss of earning power or additional expense) to which the claimant may be expected, having regard to his physical and mental condition at the date of the assessment, to be subject during the period taken into account by the assessment as compared with a person of the same age and sex whose physical and mental condition is normal;
-- src:5343 | (b) ...regulations may make provision as to the extent (if any) to which any disabilities are to be taken into account where they are disabilities which, though resulting from the relevant loss of faculty, also result, or without the relevant accident might have been expected to result, from a cause other than the relevant accident;
@ref sch 6 para 1(a) and (b) (src:5341-5343)
GIVEN `the claimant is subject to the disability as a result of the relevant loss of faculty, compared with a person of the same age and sex whose physical and mental condition is normal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant may be expected to be subject to it during the period taken into account by the assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involves loss of earning power or additional expense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it also results, or without the relevant accident might have been expected to result, from a cause other than the relevant accident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations under paragraph 1(b) provide that it is taken into account` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 1(a) the disability is taken into account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the claimant is subject to the disability as a result of the relevant loss of faculty, compared with a person of the same age and sex whose physical and mental condition is normal` AND `it also results, or without the relevant accident might have been expected to result, from a cause other than the relevant accident`
            THEN `regulations under paragraph 1(b) provide that it is taken into account`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) when NOTHING: "regulations may make provision as to the extent (if any)"
        IF `the claimant is subject to the disability as a result of the relevant loss of faculty, compared with a person of the same age and sex whose physical and mental condition is normal` AND `the claimant may be expected to be subject to it during the period taken into account by the assessment`
            THEN JUST TRUE   -- "whether or not involving loss of earning power or additional expense": the input `it involves loss of earning power or additional expense` is read by nothing
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the disabilities to be taken into account shall be all disabilities so incurred ... to which the claimant may be expected ... to be subject during the period taken into account"

-- 1(c) (read with paragraph 2): the assessment is made without reference to the particular circumstances of the claimant other than
-- age, sex, and physical and mental condition. Paragraph 2 says nothing in 1(c) prevents regulations making different provision for
-- right-handed and left-handed persons in the case of loss of faculty in or affecting hand or arm.
DECLARE `sch 6 Circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `sch 6 para 1(c) the claimant's age`
    `sch 6 para 1(c) the claimant's sex`
    `sch 6 para 1(c) the claimant's physical condition`
    `sch 6 para 1(c) the claimant's mental condition`
    `sch 6 para 2 the claimant's being right-handed or left-handed`
    `sch 6 para 1(c) any other particular circumstance of the claimant`

-- src:5344 | (c) the assessment shall be made without reference to the particular circumstances of the claimant other than age, sex, and physical and mental condition;
-- src:5346 | Provision may be made by regulations for further defining the principles on which the extent of disablement is to be assessed and such regulations may in particular direct that a prescribed loss of faculty shall be treated as resulting in a prescribed degree of disablement; and, in connection with any such direction, nothing in paragraph 1(c) above prevents the making of different provision, in the case of loss of faculty in or affecting hand or arm, for right-handed and for left-handed persons.
@ref sch 6 para 1(c) and para 2 (the handedness limb) (src:5344) (src:5346)
GIVEN circumstance IS A `sch 6 Circumstance`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 1(c) the assessment may refer to the circumstance` MEANS
    CONSIDER circumstance
    WHEN `sch 6 para 1(c) the claimant's age` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 6 para 1(c) the claimant's sex` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 6 para 1(c) the claimant's physical condition` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 6 para 1(c) the claimant's mental condition` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 6 para 2 the claimant's being right-handed or left-handed` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): only regulations under paragraph 2 can make different provision for right-handed and left-handed persons, and only for loss of faculty in or affecting hand or arm
    WHEN `sch 6 para 1(c) any other particular circumstance of the claimant` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the assessment shall be made without reference to the particular circumstances of the claimant other than age, sex, and physical and mental condition"

-- 1(d): the disabilities resulting from a loss of faculty that regulations prescribe are taken as 100 per cent disablement; other
-- disabilities are assessed accordingly. This is the answer other provisions ask of Schedule 6 (seam S21): the percentage the disabilities
-- taken into account amount to is an open-textured judgment of the assessor, taken as a plain input.
-- src:5345 | (d) the disabilities resulting from such loss of faculty as may be prescribed shall be taken as amounting to 100 per cent. disablement and other disabilities shall be assessed accordingly.
@ref sch 6 para 1(d) (src:5345)
GIVEN `the loss of faculty is one that regulations prescribe as amounting to 100 per cent disablement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the percentage the disabilities taken into account amount to` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 6 the extent of the disablement assessed, as a percentage` MEANS
    IF `the loss of faculty is one that regulations prescribe as amounting to 100 per cent disablement`
    THEN JUST 100   -- 1(d): "shall be taken as amounting to 100 per cent. disablement"
    ELSE `the percentage the disabilities taken into account amount to`   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term) when NOTHING: "disabilities ... assessed accordingly" is the assessor's judgment

§§ `Paragraphs 2 and 3 -- further definition of the principles; adjusting earlier assessments`

-- 2: regulations may further define the principles and direct that a prescribed loss of faculty is treated as a prescribed degree of
-- disablement: a regulation-making power, inert (machinery); its one limit on 1(c) (handedness) is the sixth constructor above.

-- 3: regulations may adjust or review an assessment made before the regulations came into force, with effect from that date, "so however
-- that no assessment shall be reduced by virtue of this paragraph".
-- src:5347 | Regulations under paragraph 1(d) or 2 above may include provision—
-- src:5348 | (a) for adjusting or reviewing an assessment made before the date of the coming into force of those regulations;
-- src:5349 | (b) for any resulting alteration of that assessment to have effect as from that date;
-- src:5350 | so however that no assessment shall be reduced by virtue of this paragraph.
@ref sch 6 para 3 (src:5347-5350)
GIVEN `the existing assessment, as a percentage` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage the adjustment under the regulations gives` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 6 para 3 the assessment after the adjustment` MEANS
    IF `the percentage the adjustment under the regulations gives` LESS THAN `the existing assessment, as a percentage`
    THEN `the existing assessment, as a percentage`   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no assessment shall be reduced by virtue of this paragraph"
    ELSE `the percentage the adjustment under the regulations gives`

§§ `Paragraphs 4 and 5 -- severe disablement allowance (blank in this text)`

§§ `Paragraph 6 -- disablement benefit: the period taken into account`

-- 6(1): the period to be taken into account begins not earlier than the end of the 90 days (disregarding Sundays) from the accident and
-- is limited by reference to the claimant's life or a definite date, during which the claimant has suffered and may be expected to
-- continue to suffer from the relevant loss of faculty. The first day the period may begin is the day after the 90 days (Schedule 7 para 9(3)).
-- src:5355 | (1) Subject to sub-paragraphs (2) and (3) below, the period to be taken into account by an assessment for the purposes of section 103 above and Part II of Schedule 7 to this Act of the extent of a claimant’s disablement shall be the period (beginning not earlier than the end of the period of 90 days referred to in section 103(6) above and in paragraph 9(3) of that Schedule and limited by reference either to the claimant’s life or to a definite date) during which the claimant has suffered and may be expected to continue to suffer from the relevant loss of faculty.
@ref sch 6 para 6(1) (src:5355)
GIVEN `the day of the relevant accident` IS A DATE
      `the period during which the claimant has suffered and may be expected to continue to suffer from the relevant loss of faculty` IS A Period
GIVETH A Period
`sch 6 para 6(1) the period taken into account by the assessment` MEANS
    Period WITH
        `the first day` IS later
        `the last day` IS `the period during which the claimant has suffered and may be expected to continue to suffer from the relevant loss of faculty`'s `the last day`
    WHERE
        suffering MEANS `the period during which the claimant has suffered and may be expected to continue to suffer from the relevant loss of faculty`'s `the first day`
        earliest MEANS `sch 7 pt II para 9(3) the first day after the 90 days` `the day of the relevant accident`
        later MEANS IF suffering GREATER THAN earliest THEN suffering ELSE earliest

-- 6(2): if the claimant's condition does not allow a final assessment up to the end of the period in 6(1), (a) a provisional assessment
-- is made, for a shorter period that seems reasonable, and (b) the next assessment's period begins with the end of the period taken into
-- account by the provisional assessment (read as the day after it: NOTES.md, F7). A failed "If" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a)).
-- src:5356 | (2) If on any assessment the condition of the claimant is not such, having regard to the possibility of changes in that condition (whether predictable or not), as to allow of a final assessment being made up to the end of the period provided by sub-paragraph (1) above, then, subject to sub-paragraph (3) below—
-- src:5357 | (a) a provisional assessment shall be made, taking into account such shorter period only as seems reasonable having regard to his condition and that possibility; and
-- src:5358 | (b) on the next assessment the period to be taken into account shall begin with the end of the period taken into account by the provisional assessment.
@ref sch 6 para 6(2) (src:5356-5358)
GIVEN `the claimant’s condition allows of a final assessment being made up to the end of the period provided by sub-paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 6(2) a provisional assessment is made` MEANS
    IF `the claimant’s condition allows of a final assessment being made up to the end of the period provided by sub-paragraph (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If on any assessment the condition of the claimant is not such ... as to allow of a final assessment" (a failed "if")
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:5358 | (b) on the next assessment the period to be taken into account shall begin with the end of the period taken into account by the provisional assessment.
@ref sch 6 para 6(2)(b) (src:5358)
GIVEN `the period taken into account by the provisional assessment` IS A Period
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 6 para 6(2)(b) the day the period taken into account by the next assessment begins` MEANS
    `the period taken into account by the provisional assessment`'s `the last day` PLUS 1

-- 6(3), (4), (5): an assessment of less than 14 per cent is a final assessment, whose period does not end before the earliest date on
-- which the extent seems likely to be less than 1 per cent; but (4) not where the extent seems likely to be aggregated with a present
-- disablement to 14 per cent or more; and (5) where different percentages are assessed for different parts of the period, (3) applies only
-- if the percentage for the latest part is under 14 per cent, and then only to that part.
-- src:5359 | (3) Where the assessed extent of a claimant’s disablement amounts to less than 14 per cent., then, subject to sub-paragraphs (4) and (5) below, that assessment shall be a final assessment and the period to be taken into account by it shall not end before the earliest date on which it seems likely that the extent of the disablement will be less than 1 per cent.
-- src:5360 | (4) Sub-paragraph (3) above does not apply in any case where it seems likely that—
-- src:5361 | (a) the assessed extent of the disablement will be aggregated with the assessed extent of any present disablement, and
-- src:5362 | (b) that aggregate will amount to 14 per cent. or more.
-- src:5363 | (5) Where the extent of the claimant’s disablement is assessed at different percentages for different parts of the period taken into account by the assessment, then—
-- src:5364 | (a) sub-paragraph (3) above does not apply in relation to the assessment unless the percentage assessed for the latest part of that period is less than 14 per cent., and
-- src:5365 | (b) in any such case that sub-paragraph shall apply only in relation to that part of that period (and subject to sub-paragraph (4) above).
@ref sch 6 para 6(3), (4) and (5) (src:5359-5365)
GIVEN `the assessed extent of the disablement, as a percentage` IS A NUMBER
      `the extent is assessed at different percentages for different parts of the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the percentage assessed for the latest part of the period` IS A NUMBER
      `it seems likely that the assessed extent will be aggregated with the assessed extent of any present disablement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it seems likely that the aggregate will amount to 14 per cent or more` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 6(3) the assessment is a final assessment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it seems likely that the assessed extent will be aggregated with the assessed extent of any present disablement` AND `it seems likely that the aggregate will amount to 14 per cent or more`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Sub-paragraph (3) above does not apply in any case where it seems likely that (a) ... aggregated ... and (b) ... 14 per cent. or more"
        IF `the extent is assessed at different percentages for different parts of the period` AND (`the percentage assessed for the latest part of the period` AT LEAST 14)
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "sub-paragraph (3) above does not apply in relation to the assessment unless the percentage assessed for the latest part of that period is less than 14 per cent."
        IF `the extent is assessed at different percentages for different parts of the period`
            THEN JUST TRUE   -- the answer is then about the latest part only, whatever the percentage of the other parts; 6(5)(b): "in any such case that sub-paragraph shall apply only in relation to that part of that period"
        IF `the assessed extent of the disablement, as a percentage` LESS THAN 14
            THEN JUST TRUE   -- 6(3): "that assessment shall be a final assessment"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the assessed extent ... amounts to less than 14 per cent." says nothing of an extent of 14 per cent or more

-- 6(3): the period to be taken into account by such a final assessment shall not end before the earliest date on which it seems likely
-- that the extent of the disablement will be less than 1 per cent.
-- src:5359 | (3) Where the assessed extent of a claimant’s disablement amounts to less than 14 per cent., then, subject to sub-paragraphs (4) and (5) below, that assessment shall be a final assessment and the period to be taken into account by it shall not end before the earliest date on which it seems likely that the extent of the disablement will be less than 1 per cent.
@ref sch 6 para 6(3) (src:5359)
GIVEN `the earliest date on which it seems likely that the extent of the disablement will be less than 1 per cent` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period taken into account` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 6(3) the period taken into account may end on the day` MEANS
    IF `the last day of the period taken into account` LESS THAN `the earliest date on which it seems likely that the extent of the disablement will be less than 1 per cent`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the period to be taken into account by it shall not end before the earliest date on which it seems likely that the extent of the disablement will be less than 1 per cent."
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall not end before" says nothing of an end on or after that date

§§ `Paragraph 7 -- what an assessment states`

-- 7: an assessment shall (a) state the degree of disablement as a percentage, (b) specify the period taken into account and (c) where
-- that period is limited by reference to a definite date, specify whether it is provisional or final; but the percentage and the period
-- shall not be specified more particularly than is necessary for determining the claimant's rights under section 103 and Schedule 7.
-- src:5366 | An assessment for the purposes of section 103 above and Part II of Schedule 7 to this Act shall—
-- src:5367 | (a) state the degree of disablement in the form of a percentage;
-- src:5368 | (b) specify the period taken into account by the assessment; and
-- src:5369 | (c) where that period is limited by reference to a definite date, specify whether the assessment is provisional or final;
@ref sch 6 para 7(a), (b) and (c) (src:5366-5369)
GIVEN `the period is limited by reference to a definite date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`sch 6 para 7 what the assessment must state` MEANS
    IF `the period is limited by reference to a definite date`
    THEN LIST
        "the degree of disablement in the form of a percentage"
        "the period taken into account by the assessment"
        "whether the assessment is provisional or final"
    ELSE LIST
        "the degree of disablement in the form of a percentage"
        "the period taken into account by the assessment"

-- src:5370 | but the percentage and the period shall not be specified more particularly than is necessary for the purpose of determining in accordance with section 103 above and Parts II and IV of Schedule 7 to this Act the claimant’s rights as to disablement pension or gratuity and reduced earnings allowance (whether or not a claim has been made).
@ref sch 6 para 7 (src:5370)
GIVEN `the particularity is necessary for determining the claimant’s rights as to disablement pension or gratuity and reduced earnings allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 7 the percentage and the period may be specified more particularly` MEANS
    IF `the particularity is necessary for determining the claimant’s rights as to disablement pension or gratuity and reduced earnings allowance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the percentage and the period shall not be specified more particularly than is necessary for the purpose of determining ... the claimant’s rights"

§§ `Paragraph 8 -- constant attendance allowance, etc.`

-- 8(1): regulations may provide how the extent of disablement is determined for an increase under section 104 (constant attendance) or
-- the corresponding increase under Schedule 8: a regulation-making power, inert (machinery).
-- 8(2): the payments whose injuries count, if regulations so provide, are disablement pension, benefit under paragraph 4 or 7(1) of
-- Schedule 8, and such other benefit as is prescribed in connection with hostilities or service in the forces. The list ends with "or" and
-- is not closed by "only", so a payment outside it is not covered.
DECLARE `sch 6 Payment` IS ONE OF
    `sch 6 para 8(2)(a) a payment by way of disablement pension`
    `sch 6 para 8(2)(b) a payment by way of benefit under paragraph 4 or 7(1) of Schedule 8`
    `sch 6 para 8(2)(c) a payment of other prescribed benefit in connection with hostilities or service as a member of Her Majesty’s forces or of another specified organisation`
    `sch 6 para 8(2) any other payment`

-- src:5376 | (2) Those payments are—
-- src:5377 | (a) payments by way of disablement pension;
-- src:5378 | (b) payments by way of benefit under paragraph 4 or 7(1) of Schedule 8 to this Act; or
-- src:5379 | (c) payments in such circumstances as may be prescribed by way of such other benefit as may be prescribed (being benefit in connection with any hostilities or with service as a member of Her Majesty’s forces or of such other organisation as may be specified in the regulations).
@ref sch 6 para 8(2) (src:5376-5379)
GIVEN payment IS A `sch 6 Payment`
      `the benefit is prescribed, in the circumstances, under paragraph 8(2)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 8(2) the payment is one of those payments` MEANS
    CONSIDER payment
    WHEN `sch 6 para 8(2)(a) a payment by way of disablement pension` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 6 para 8(2)(b) a payment by way of benefit under paragraph 4 or 7(1) of Schedule 8` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 6 para 8(2)(c) a payment of other prescribed benefit in connection with hostilities or service as a member of Her Majesty’s forces or of another specified organisation` THEN
        IF `the benefit is prescribed, in the circumstances, under paragraph 8(2)(c)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "in such circumstances as may be prescribed ... such other benefit as may be prescribed"
    WHEN `sch 6 para 8(2) any other payment` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Those payments are— (a) ... (b) ... or (c) ..." is not closed by "only"
